    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Let me break it down for you in plain language.\n\nIn Toronto, the escrow account is typically held by a third-party escrow agent, such as a title company or a mortgage broker. This agent is responsible for holding the funds until the closing date, when they are released to the seller as per the terms of the sale.\n\nThe escrow agent is usually a reputable and licensed company, and they have a fiduciary duty to hold the funds in trust. This means that they are required to follow specific rules and regulations to ensure that the funds are handled properly.\n\nTo ensure that the escrow agent is trustworthy, you can check their credentials and reviews. You can also ask your realtor or lender to recommend a reputable escrow agent.\n\nAs for the risk of the escrow agent losing the money, it's relatively low. Escrow agents are required to maintain a separate account for the escrow funds, which are usually held in a separate bank account. This account is typically insured by the Canadian Deposit Insurance Corporation (CDIC), which protects deposits up to $100,000.\n\nAdditionally, escrow agents are required to follow strict guidelines and regulations to ensure that the funds are",
